CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The instantiation scope of a template uses the namespace enclosing the
template (sub_scope_for_instantiation), and lookup searched that using
scope before the template parameter scope, so `B' in enable_if_t's body
found the later namespace-scope `using B = binder<...>' instead of the
parameter.
